* §30.3(i): `(1-z²)^{m/2} g(z)` solves 30.2.1 with `μ = m` iff `g` solves the factor equation;
* §30.12: the generalized equations 30.12.1 and 30.12.2 reduce to 30.2.1 at `α = 0` (proved).

# Estimates for the Mellin–Barnes integrand of the Struve function

Tools for the Barnes integral of `H_ν` (DLMF 11.5.8), whose integrand on `s = t + iy` is
`π/sin(πs) · w^s / (Γ(3/2+s) Γ(3/2+ν+s))`:

* `struveBar_recip_Gamma_isBigO`: on a shifted vertical line,
  `1/|Γ(a + i(y+m))| = O(y^{1/2-a} e^{πy/2})` as `y → +∞` (Stirling, DLMF 5.11.9, from
  `DLMF.Gamma.tendsto_norm_Gamma_vertical_div`);
* `struveBar_pi_div_sin_le`, `struveBar_pi_div_sin_isBigO`: `π/|sin(π(t+iy))| ≤ 4π e^{-πy}`
  for `y ≥ 1`;
* `struveBar_isBigO`: the product `π/|sin| · 1/|Γ(a+iy)| · 1/|Γ(b+i(y+m))|` is `O(y^{1-a-b})`;
* `struveBar_integrableOn_rpow_div_Gamma`: `w^t/(Γ(α+t)Γ(β+t))` is integrable on `(c, ∞)`;
* `struveBar_integrable_of_isBigO`: continuous functions with `O(|y|^p)` tails, `p < -1`, are
  integrable on `ℝ`.

# Poisson integrals for the Struve functions

Termwise Beta integration of the Struve series against the Poisson weight
`(1-t²)^(ν-1/2)` on `[0,1]` (DLMF 11.5.1, 11.5.4, 11.5.6):

* `integral_poissonWeight_mul_pow`: the Beta moments `∫₀¹ (1-t²)^(ν-1/2) t^m dt`;
* `hasSum_integral_poissonWeight`: termwise integration of a power series on `[0,1]`;
* `integral_poissonWeight_eq_trig`: the substitution `t = cos θ`;
* `struveH_eq_poisson`, `struveL_eq_poisson`, `struveM_eq_poisson`.

The `I_ν` case reuses `DLMF.Bessel.besselI_eq_poisson_integral`.

# Theta functions (DLMF Chapter 20)

The Jacobi theta functions `θⱼ(z|τ)` are `DLMF.Elliptic.jacobiThetaOneTau … jacobiThetaFourTau`
(DLMF normalization, from Mathlib's `jacobiTheta₂`). This area acquires DLMF §§20.2, 20.4–20.11:

* `Basic`: nome forms `θⱼ(z,q)`, theta constants, Fourier series, quasi-periodicity, half-period
  translations and zeros (§§20.1–20.2);
* `ZeroValues`: values and derivatives at `z = 0` (§20.4);
* `Products`: single and double products, triple product, logarithmic derivatives (§20.5);
* `PowerSeries`: exponential power series and lattice sums (§20.6);
* `Identities`: sums of squares, addition, duplication, Landen, Watson, lattice-parameter
  transformations (§20.7) and Watson's expansion (§20.8);
* `Relations`: elliptic integrals, Jacobi's inversion problem, the modular function (§20.9);
* `Integrals`: Mellin and Laplace transforms in the lattice parameter (§20.10);
* `Generalizations`: Gauss sums, Ramanujan's `f(a,b)`, change of base, Carlson's combined theta
  functions (§20.11);
* `MathlibCoverage`: checked pointers to Mathlib.

The ledger is `DLMF20Acquisition.md`.

# Scalar power series: uniqueness of coefficients and the exponential series

* `FormalMultilinearSeries.eq_ofScalars_coeff`: a one-variable series is `ofScalars` of its
  coefficients;
* `Complex.eq_zero_of_hasSum_mul_pow_ball`, `Complex.eq_of_hasSum_mul_pow_ball`: the
  coefficients of a scalar power series are determined by its sums on a small disk;
* `Complex.hasSum_pow_div_factorial`, `Real.hasSum_pow_div_factorial`: the exponential
  series;
* `Complex.ne_zero_of_hasSum_ofReal_of_nonneg`: a series of nonnegative reals with positive
  leading term has nonzero sum.

# Values and basic identities of the complex Gamma function

* `Complex.Gamma_one_half_eq_sqrt`: `Γ(1/2) = √π`, with the real square root;
* `Complex.Gamma_one_half_sub_nat_mul_factorial`: `Γ(1/2 - s) (2s)! = (-4)^s s! √π`;
* `Complex.pi_mul_inv_Gamma_mul_inv_Gamma_one_sub`: `π / (Γ(s) Γ(1-s)) = sin (π s)`
  for every `s`, including the poles;
* `Complex.analyticAt_Gamma`: `Γ` is analytic off the nonpositive integers;
* the everywhere convergent series of the regularized `₀F₁`.

# Elementary exponential bounds for trigonometric and hyperbolic functions

* `Complex.norm_sin_le_exp_abs_im`, `Complex.norm_cos_le_exp_abs_im`:
  `‖sin z‖, ‖cos z‖ ≤ e^{|Im z|}`;
* `Real.cosh_le_exp_abs`: `cosh t ≤ e^{|t|}`;
* `Real.exp_sub_one_le_mul_exp`: `eʸ - 1 ≤ y eʸ`;
* `Real.cos_pos_of_abs_lt_pi_div_two` and its partial converse
  `Real.abs_lt_pi_div_two_of_cos_pos`.

